From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akramboussanni <92455979+akramboussanni@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:19:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] macos: Take prayer times from Kimono instead of Mawaqit and
 AlAdhan
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Why: Kimono Prayer already looks up Mawaqit, MasjidBox and calculated times on
the server and remembers each person's place across their devices. The menu bar
app should show exactly that, not scrape mawaqit.net or call AlAdhan itself.

What must survive upstream changes:
- Network.swift is KimonoService, and it is the only thing that goes online.
  Everything goes through SavedState.link:
    GET <link>                        -> { place, timetable, recent, problem? }
    GET <link>?q=<text>               -> { places }  (words, a mosque link, "lat, lon")
    GET <link>?lat=&lon=&tz=<IANA>    -> { places }  (the location button; tz is the Mac's)
    PUT <link> {"id"}                 -> same as GET (choosing a result)
  Non-200 answers carry { error }, shown as the status. 401 means the link was
  renewed: the link is forgotten (times kept) and the status says to connect
  again from Kimono Prayer.
- No mawaqit.net, AlAdhan or other source URL is left in Sources: the Mawaqit
  page parser, slug parser and AlAdhan parser are gone, and so is the separate
  "Use calculated prayer times" option (calculated places come back as search
  results).
- KimonoTimetable.prayerCalendar() turns timetable.days into upstream's
  PrayerCalendar (calendar[month - 1]["<day>"] = the six times). ScheduleBuilder,
  the highlighting, night milestones, countdown title, notifications and every
  other view of the schedule are upstream's, unchanged. The once-a-year refresh
  gate is dropped: the feed spans the new year by itself.
- SavedState keeps the Kimono place (id, kind, name, detail, url), not a slug or
  a calculation query. The panel names the place, its source reads
  "Kimono · Mawaqit" / "MasjidBox" / "Calculated", Settings says where the
  times come from (and the place's detail, e.g. the calculation method).
- It refreshes on launch, then hourly while connected (so a place chosen on
  another device shows up), and on Refresh.
- Tests cover decoding the feed, the conversion across a year end, and
  refusing unreadable days.

